+++ b/ops/changelog.md
@@ -9333,3 +9333,4 @@ Did NOT modify research-roadmap.yaml or scripts/research_conductor.py. Did NOT p
 - 2026-06-18: PHASE B1 (ARC NORTH STAR; operator MANDATORY 2026-06-17; biggest reproducible-level upside) -- E3 DEEPER on the high-headroom cracked games via per-mechanic EXECUTABLE UNIT TESTS that DECOMPOSE the lookahead-fidelity blocker (Mind-Studio arXiv:2606.16070): lp85 L6 + tu93 L5 + tn36 L8 + tr87 L7, +1 each per Incremental-Progress Scoping. .406 (exp4394) gated planning on AGGREGATE lookahead-fidelity and STALLED -- fidelity 0.80-0.875, UNREACHABLE, 0 new levels -- because an aggregate gate only CONFIRMS the blocker, it does not tell you WHICH transition the world model gets wrong. This attempt's STATED forward difference: DECOMPOSE the fidelity failure into per-mechanic EXECUTABLE UNIT TESTS -- for each game, run the world model's K-step rollout against the env, identify the SPECIFIC mismatched transition(s), write an executable unit test asserting the correct transition, FIX the engine to pass that test (an InT-style targeted intervention on the world model), and only THEN re-check fidelity + plan deeper. Report per-mechanic test pass/fail SEPARATELY from any solve claim. Entropy-selected exploration traces + a lightweight per-game skill file. LOOP the four targets with a per-target checkpoint + hard per-target wall-time cap (breadth-of-progress beats all-or-nothing). The codex agent IS the proposer (NO nested CodexProposer). HARD gate per target: a NEW level offline_reproduced=true beyond the prior reproduced best (arc_solver_kit.reproduce). Report a per-target scorecard + the new reproducible_total_levels. An honest partial per target (the per-mechanic unit tests that now PASS + the residual failing-mechanic test as the gap CLASS) is PROGRESS. verifier_is_oracle=true (execution-grounded). NO TRM training; NO leaderboard submission; checkpoint after EACH target. (⚠️ Research Finding) — honest_verdict=complete_e3_deeper_partial; results/experiment_4405_e3_deeper_mechanic_unit_tests.json
 - 2026-06-18: PHASE B2 (ARC NORTH STAR; operator MANDATORY 2026-06-17; close the named hidden-rule gaps) -- E3 the BLOCKED-mechanic next-levels via per-mechanic EXECUTABLE UNIT TESTS on the NAMED registers (arXiv:2606.16070): ar25 L2 (action7 undo-stack) + ka59 L2 (step-counter HUD + object-RELEVANCE) + ft09 L2, +1 each per Incremental-Progress Scoping. ar25 L1 + ka59 L1 + ft09 L1 are SOLVED; the next levels are blocked on NAMED hidden-rule gaps. exp4395 (.406) added a per-register lookahead-fidelity gate and produced NO new levels (fidelity stuck below the gate). This attempt's STATED forward difference: write an EXECUTABLE UNIT TEST for each NAMED hidden-rule register (ar25 action7 undo-stack restores the prior grid; ka59 the step-counter HUD increments iff the RELEVANT object's state changes -- the outer-loop's object-RELEVANCE finding, commits f0b078247/6fba583c7; ft09 the residual transition), FIX the world model to pass each test, and only then plan. The codex agent IS the proposer (NO nested CodexProposer). HARD gate per game: a NEW level offline_reproduced=true beyond the prior best. An honest partial per game (the per-register unit tests that now PASS + the residual failing-register test as the sharper gap CLASS) is PROGRESS. verifier_is_oracle=true (execution-grounded). NO TRM training; NO leaderboard submission; checkpoint after EACH game. (⚠️ Research Finding) — honest_verdict=complete_e3_ar25_ka59_ft09_partial; results/experiment_4406_e3_blocked_mechanic_tails_unit_tests.json
 - 2026-06-18: PHASE C (CONTINUOUS SELF-LEARNING; mandated per research-program.md; verifier_is_oracle=false) -- does ACTIVE-LEARNING trace selection produce COMPOUNDING where the .406 SIZE-only growth SATURATED? (ActPRM arXiv:2504.10559). .406 (exp4396) grew the first-error corpus by SIZE alone and saturated (learning curve F1=1.0 FLAT 566->5661, localizer_compounds=false) -- but that was on the ARTIFACT-confounded synthetic localizer (no real headroom). The NEW mechanism: ACTIVE selection -- pick the next traces to label by UNCERTAINTY (the localizer's least-confident first-error predictions) + first-error-POSITION DIVERSITY (cover under-represented positions, NOT just add more of the same), and measure held-out first-error F1 vs the accumulated-corpus SIZE as an ACTIVE-vs-RANDOM learning curve. Run on the BEST available first-error localizer: exp4403's REAL-intervention localizer if it is genuine, ELSE the deconfounded real-intervention corpus from exp4403 (the question is whether ACTIVE selection breaks the saturation that SIZE-only growth could not). Keep the template-family holdout + a content-blind position-only control IN the active loop (so 'compounding' is not re-learning the artifact). Emit localizer_compounds BARE bool := (held-out first-error F1 under ACTIVE selection RISES with corpus size BEYOND a RANDOM-selection baseline at the same corpus size, delta CI95-excl-0, with a positive control confirming non-trivial ceiling headroom). verifier_is_oracle=false. A win = the localizer COMPOUNDS via active selection (the self-learning headline on the axis that now has real headroom); a clean null (active selection does not beat random -> the localizer's signal is saturated or position-bound) is decision-grade. Cached candidates, CPU, zero quota. NO TRM training. (✅ Complete) — honest_verdict=complete: clean_null_position_bound_or_saturated; results/experiment_4407_active_learning_self_learning_compounds.json
+- 2026-06-18: PHASE D (CROSS-DOMAIN DETECTION CALIBRATION; complementary; cached; verifier_is_oracle=false) -- REPAIR the .406 false calibrated-multi-domain detector contract with PROPER pools + base-rate separation (Semantic Confidence Aggregation arXiv:2602.07842). .406 (exp4397) reported detection_calibrated_multi_domain=false, but the failure was CONFOUNDED: code_humaneval detection AUROC was 0.98 yet underpowered (n=100) and the multi-valid-output / base-rate effects were not separated from genuine calibration failure. This attempt: (1) build PROPER pools from EXISTING cached candidates -- code (HumanEval, cached exp1999/2838/2839, n>=300) + GSM8K (cached, n>=300) -- NOT the underpowered n=100; (2) apply SEMANTIC CONFIDENCE AGGREGATION (aggregate the verifier's confidence across semantically-equivalent valid answers / verifier-success modes BEFORE calibration) + per-domain BASE-RATE + answer-cardinality metadata, so calibration failure is separated from multi-valid-output/base-rate effects; (3) leave-one-domain-out calibration (Platt/temperature fit on the other domains) and report detection AUROC + risk-coverage + expected-calibration-error per domain. Emit detection_calibrated_multi_domain BARE bool := (detection AUROC CI95 lower bound > 0.5 on >=2 NON-FoVer domains AND leave-one-domain-out calibration keeps ECE below the uncalibrated baseline on the held-out domain, AFTER base-rate/multi-valid separation). verifier_is_oracle=false. A win = a deployable multi-domain detector contract (the verifier-domain-expansion step, north-star §0 step 2); a domain at chance is LOGGED as a missing-verifier gap (the product backlog). This is cross-domain DETECTION (AUROC), NOT the RETIRED cross-domain SELECTION axis (exp4314). Cached candidates, CPU, zero quota. NO new live inference; NO TRM training. (✅ Complete) — honest_verdict=complete: calibrated_multi_domain_contract_false_deconfounded; results/experiment_4408_cross_domain_detection_calibration_repair.json
